Hello,

I'd like to announce the release of a new version of xwb,
which means X-window workbench, an editing tool. When 
loading a source file it detects the type by extension
and sets up the compile/run program menu automatically.
Pre-configured are C/C++, TeX, HTML, POV and many other
source files types - new ones can be added.
And it's (I think) easy to use for beginners, too..
I used the Xview+Xlib library as the GUI.
It's free available with source code under the terms of GPL.


The primary sites to get it are:

    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/x11/xapps/editors
(where it'll be moved from
    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming)
(use a mirror site)
as well as
    http://WWW.FH-Karlsruhe.de/~somi0011/s_soft_html/s_soft..html


The main changes are:
 Lots of bugfixes (runs very stable on my machine)
 Ported to Sun Solaris.
 Starting grep from Menu and 
  diff with edited file & its backup.
 Insertion of columns and remove a column - case sensitive with given
string
  at the beginning or the end of a line (un-/commenting, adding column of
spaces).
 Fixed problems with filechooser.
 Multiple file in source format.
 Readonly comment with readonly files 




Greetings, Michael


P.S. The name Schlampisoft(NR) is not a real company name - it's
     just an alias for programs written by be.
     
     
     
