[ Moderator's note: XBanner is a program for making fancy login screens
  for xdm (and possibly for other similar purposes). --liw ]

Hello!

Another bug was found in the Makefile as is distributed in the XBanner 1.2
archive. In simple words:

If you have downloaded XBanner 1.2, do not run 'make install'!

Simply copy the files manually. The bug is that the install command
overwrites the XBanner binary. To fix this, locate the line in the
Makefile that says:

 $(INSTALL) --strip --mode "0755" --owner root --group bin xb_check
	/usr/local/bin/xbanner

As you can see, this line overwrites the xbanner binary with the xb_check
binary...

This will be fixed in the coming release of XBanner v1.3, which should be
available sometime soon, with many many new options.

If you don't know what XBanner is, try URL:

http://chaos.fullerton.edu/XBanner/

	Amit Margalit

