machine by referring to it as a "stove", furnace, heater, power-grid-killer,
etc?

Are you having too many unexplained "signal 11" messages on your 6x86 system?

Do you like to fiddle with hardware to see how long it takes to find the
register that hangs the thing ?


In that case, this utility might not help:

Begin3
Title: Cyrix/IBM/SGS-Thomson/... 5x86/6x86 CPU configuration tool
Version: 1.0
Entered-date: 6 AUG 96
Description: Allows one to modify the internal configuration registers in
             the 5x86 and 6x86 CPU. These include specifying non-cacheable
             memory areas (important for e.g. graphics cards), I/O delays,
             cache write policy (WB/WT), and also enable an automatic
             standby mode where a CPU "halt" instruction cuts down power by
             a factor of 70 (from 20 Watts to 0.3 Watts for the 6x86 P133+)
             when the CPU is idle. Especially the CPU power reduction cuts
             down on most temperature-related problems (crashes, "signal
             11",...) on many motherboards.
