		InfoMagic Workgroup Server Fact-Sheet

The InfoMagic Workgroup Server provides high-performance file and
printing services to PC and Macintosh clients using the Linux
operating system. It is the first Linux distribution designed
specifically for servers. Based on networking software created by the
Internet community and already in use at hundreds of companies,
universities and organizations worldwide, the InfoMagic Workgroup
Server provides simple graphical tools for system administration and
set-up. A Unix novice can set up a sophisticated server environment
in a couple of hours.

The InfoMagic Workgroup Server is available in two versions:

Unsupported - A mailing list is provided to post questions
regarding the installation and use of the product. Support is
available for the first 30 days via this list. 

  Price $75.00

Supported - If you feel the Workgroup Server is critical to your
organization you will want to purchase a support contract with
InfoMagic. This contract entitles you to call, FAX, or email your
questions. This contract provides you with up to 5 hours of support
and may be renewed anually. For other support options please contact
us. 

  Price $499.00

For additional information or to order contact InfoMagic in any of
the following wasys:

Phone:	800-800-6613 (US & Canada) or 520-526-9565
FAX:	520-526-9573
EMail:	Orders@InfoMagic.com
WWW:	http://www.infomagic.com/


Of course, the InfoMagic Workgroup Server includes Linux's well-known
support for Internet services, enabling a single machine to provide
World Wide Web, email, and Internet connectivity (TCP/IP routing, PPP
and SLIP dial-up) services while simultaneously acting as a PC and
Macintosh server.

Features:
  PC Services

	Works with any Windows for Workgroups, Windows 95, Windows NT, OS/2
	or DOS machine (or any other SMB-TCP/IP client) with no
	server-specific software on the client machine and no client license
	charges.

	Clients can mount server file directories using the usual
	mechanisms--e.g. the File Manager in Windows for Workgroups--and
	access server disk space totally transparently.

	Clients can connect to server print queues and print to them as if
	printing to a locally- connected printer.

  Macintosh Services

	Works with the built-in AppleTalk client software included with
	every Macintosh.

	Clients mount server disk volumes using the Chooser, and they
	then appear on the desktop ready for use by any Macintosh program.

	Clients can select server print queues in the Chooser and then
	print to them just as if printing to any other Macintosh printer.

  Cross-platform capability

	PC and Macintosh users can mount the same directories on the server
	to share files without any hassle.

	PC and Macintosh users can share one another's printers. A print
	queue on the server can represent a printer directly attached to the
	server itself, a printer attached to any other Unix host, an
	AppleTalk printer, or a shared printer attached to a PC. Any client,
	whether PC or Macintosh, can print to any queue. The result is
	universal printer access: a Macintosh user can, for example, print to
	a printer attached to a Windows for Workgroups machine, and a Windows
	95 user can print to an AppleTalk laser printer--all without any
	special software on the client side.

  Flexible set-up

	With just a few clicks, it is possible to set-up home directories
	on the server for everyone, or set up directories for collaborative
	work available just to a group of users, or set up directories
	readable by everyone but writable only by a certain group.

  Graphical administration tools

	The InfoMagic Workgroup Server includes a complete set of tools for
	installation and management which run under the X Window System using
	a Motif-like user interface:

		User and group management
		Network configuration
		Disk and file system management
		Software version management
		Printer queue management
		Startup control panel
		Directory browser
		PC sharing services configuration
		Macintosh sharing services configuration
		Graphical file system backup configuration

  Built-in Internet TCP/IP services

	The InfoMagic Workgroup Server includes high-performance Internet
	services which make an ideal complement to its native PC and
	Macintosh networking capabilities:

	Internet email, including POP and IMAP client support. the
	InfoMagic Workgroup Server users automatically get internet email
	mailboxes, which they can access from their PC or Mac using any
	internet email user agent like Eudora, ECS mail (simeon) or PC-Pine.

	A World Wide Web server. With the InfoMagic Workgroup Server, you
	can have the performance, reliability and security of running your
	web server on a full multitasking, multiuser operating system like
	Linux, while allowing Macintosh and PC users to create web documents
	using familiar tools and save them directly onto the server using the
	shared filesystems.

	Full Internet routing and dial-up capabilities. With attached
	modems, the InfoMagic Workgroup Server can provide full dialup
	Internet access using SLIP or PPP. 

  Proven software

	The InfoMagic Workgroup Server is based on software which is
	already in use at hundreds of sites worldwide, including:

		Linux version 1.2.13 kernel
		Red Hat Commercial Linux
		the "netatalk" AppleTalk package
		the "samba" PC networking package

The InfoMagic Workgroup Server combines these components in a tested
package which is easy to install and administer. 

Compatibility -- Users of Red Hat Commercial Linux or Caldera Network
Desktop can easily upgrade to the InfoMagic Workgroup Server while
retaining all the features of the underlying system.  

By combining the InfoMagic Workgroup Server with Caldera's Netware
Client, it is possible to export Netware disks and printers to PC and
Macintosh clients without requiring any Novell code on the client
machines. 

InfoMagic has not just collected archive material. The core software
was tested extensively and subtle bugs were ironed out.
The administration of these tools was carefully studied and
implemented.




