                      PROCMETER V2.0
                      ==============

A simple X based performance meter for Linux (like xmeter).
Displays statistics direct from /proc on the local machine.

The procmeter homepage is accessible via <http://www.gedanken.demon.co.uk/>
so you can see more information about the program and download it.

Available statistics are in a number of classes

Processes:

cpu         %  Total cpu usage
cpu-user    %  cpu used by user processes
cpu-nice    %  cpu used by niced processes
cpu-sys     %  cpu used by system processes
cpu-idle    %  cpu unused
load           System load
context        Number of context switches

Virtual Memory:

swap           Amount of swapping
swap-in        Amount of swap in
swap-out       Amount of swap out
page           Amount of paging
page-in        Amount of page in
page-out       Amount of page out

Hardware:

disk           Amount of disk accesses
intr           Number of interrupts

Memory:

mem-free    MB Amount of free memory
mem-used    MB Amount of used memory
mem-buff    MB Amount of file buffer memory
mem-cache   MB Amount of cached memory (kernel version >2.0)
mem-swap    MB Amount of swap space used

Network:

lpkt           Number of packets             \
lpkt-rx        Number of received packets     | 'Local' interfaces (lo and dummy).
lpkt-tx        Number of transmitted packets /
fpkt           Number of packets             \
fpkt-rx        Number of received packets     | 'Fast' interfaces (eth).
fpkt-tx        Number of transmitted packets /
spkt           Number of packets             \
spkt-rx        Number of received packets     | 'Slow' interfaces (sl and ppp).
spkt-tx        Number of transmitted packets /


New for Version 2.0
- -------------------

Almost completely rewritten compared to version 1.x.

Uses less memory and cpu than version 1.1.
Adapts the list of available statistics to those available.
Works with kernel version 2.0.


