What is cx5x86mod ?
- -------------------
It is a kernel module to fiddle with the register settings of the
Cyrix 5x86 cpu.  It is meant for those who might think that their
motherboards do not fully utilize the CPU, or those who has nothing
else better to do.  The kernel module can mess with almost every
register setting of the CPU.


Credits
- -------
This program was derived from Christopher Lau's kernel module and
patch for enabling the L1 cache in some Cyrix 486 CPUs.  However,
very little, if any, is left of the original code.  Also, assistance
from Bruce Stough <sbs1@PO6.RV.unisys.com> and Richard
<richard@radar.demon.co.uk> (apology to Richard as I can't seem to
be able to contact him via email for his family name :-( ) was
appreciated!


What's new?
- -----------
1) It _should_ work this time.  It has to.  It must.  It will.
   Last two versions were broken by last minute modifications just
   before shipping :-/

2) Patch to bogo.c from Richard so that the new bogomips is
   reflected in /proc/cpuinfo.  Hooray!

3) Fixed the irritating Unresolved Symbols message when doing
   depmod -a.


LSM
- ---
Here's the LSM entry:

