This is to announce the availability of GOMscript which is an
interpreter for an object-oriented, C++-like, language. It (currently)
runs on AIX (3.2.5, 4.1.X) and Linux ELF (tested on 1.3.53 and 2.0.0).

For a detailed description of the language see
http://www.zurich.ibm.com/~bba/gomscript.html.

The language can easily be extended by adding functions / classes in
the form of shared libraries. Two extensions are currently available:

 - Extension for 'roaming code': this allows to send code *and* state
   of a currently running script to another interpreter (for example
   located on a different machine). 
   (c.f. http://www.zurich.ibm.com/~bba/agent.html)

 - Extension for GOM (http://www.zurich.ibm.com/~bba/gom.html): This
   allows to manipulate (creation, deletion, modification of
   attributes, invocation of methods) of GOM classes. The extension
   supports IBM's DSOM CORBA implementation. I developed it
   mainly for interactively testing new DSOM classes rather than
   having to write a small client application every time. I found this
   quite useful and want to share it with others.


GOMscript is available at:

http://www.zurich.ibm.com/~bba/dsom_interpreter.html


The binaries are provided as is without any warranty for damage caused
by its use. If you find any bugs, send me an email and I will try to
fix them as time permits. For questions and feedback, send me an email as well
! (Or add yourself to my guest book at http://www.zurich.ibm.com/~bba)

Have fun !



