ftp://ftp.nada.kth.se/home/su95-kjo/knews-0.9.8.tar.gz

To install it you need an ANSI C compiler, the X libraries of
version X11R4 or greater and an OS supporting POSIX+sockets.


Here are some of the features:

+  True threading, with a graphical tree for the threads.
+  Inline images.
+  Support for reading Mime:
     *  Fonts may be set on a per-charset basis.
     *  Decoding of QP, base64 and [x-]uue[ncoded].
     *  Experimental decoding of some encodings for 16-bit charsets:
          utf-7, hz-gb-2312, ksc-5601, and big5.               
     *  Rfc1522 decoding of headers.
     *  Handles multipart/* articles.
     *  Assembly of message/partial articles.
+  Posting with attachments.
+  Some features to improve things for people reading over slow lines:
     *  Background threading + caching of thread info to disk.
     *  Doesn't have to read the active file.
     *  Caching and background pre-fetch of articles.
     *  Caching of group descriptions in a file.
+  Kill file support, with the ability to mark interesting articles,
   subjects and threads with color blobs.
+  Regular expression searching in articles and the newsgroup list.
+  Clicking on URLs.
+  Different fonts and colors for quoted text and headers in articles.
+  Very configurable.

