Hi to Linux admin/users,

This is the third public release of binstats, version 0.95 - an
administration utility for tracking down the various types of binary formats
for Linux (i386) executables and their dynamic library dependencies.

Features include:
 1) tally of a.out and ELF binaries, dynamically and statically linked,
    unstripped and setuid
 2) tally of duplicated executable names
 3) tally of binaries with missing dynamic libraries
 4) tally of DLL and ELF dynamic libraries, used and unused
 5) a log of all the above tallies plus listing a.out binaries, statically
    linked binaries, unstripped binaries, setuid binaries, duplicated
    executables, missing library binaries, all used and unused dynamic
    libraries
 6) a C program that dereferences symbolic links

It is inspired by "execount" written by Murple (murple@clark.net)
<URL:ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/utils/scripts/>.


Changes from 0.93:
  0.94 - Improved the symbolic link dereferencing to cope with some
         types of relative links on 1996/8/20

  0.95 - Written a C program, derefsymlink to do dereferencing, added
         setuid counting and beautified output on 1996/8/23


