Hello,

This is the annoucement of pre-alpha release of (unofficial) AWE32
sound driver kit for Linux.
By recent CreativeLab's change of attitude to open their secrets of
AWE32 programing, I could develop this sound driver at last :-)

This driver provides wave synth operations of Emu8000 on SB AWE32
cards like GUS driver, so you can listen to MIDI musics via your AWE
sounds (but some modifications are necessary).

The driver supports both Kernel1.2.13 (VoxWare.3.01) and Kernel2.0.x
(USS-Lite). The functions are identical in both cases.

To listen to musics, of course you have to prepare SoundFont 2 (SF2)
file, or SF1TO2.EXE converter by CreativeLab.  Please refer to the
document in the utility package.

Even though this driver is really experimental, I hope that this
stimulates many users to develop much more better drivers.

The driver source code and utility programs are found at the following
site:

