-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

                                        
                               The Linux Gazette
                   "...making Linux just a little more fun!"

ANNOUNCING:
                                        
              * * * Linux Gazette Issue #8 is Now Available! * * *


SO, YOU ASK, JUST WHAT EXACTING *IS* THE LINUX GAZETTE...?

For those of you who might be wondering... the Linux Gazette is a freely
available, online WWW document that includes a series of articles and
letters containing tips, tricks, ideas, and suggestions for customizing
and running Linux.  It is a member of the Linux Documentation Project.

In short... it attempts to make running Linux just a little more fun!

The Big News this month is that as of this issue I'll be turning the
reins of the Linux Gazette over to the very capable hands of the folks
at the Linux Journal (http://www.ssc.com/).  I decided to do this for
a variety of reasons, primarily because the Gazette has grown to a
size I never would have imagined (at last count it is mirrored at over
30 sites in 24 different countries around the world) and in so doing
has gotten beyond the time constraints that I current live with.  I'm
indebted to Phil Hughes and all the folks at LJ for being willing to 
take on this project -- and YES, it'll continue as it always has -- a
bit free form and rambly here and there, and hopefully, a LOT of fun!

Anyway, that's the Big News... :-)


AVAILABILITY:

So, the new home for the Linux Gazette is now at SSC!  I've uploaded 
this latest issue to them and in a day or so it should be available
for ftp at:

ftp://ftp.ssc.com/pub/lg/lg_issue8.tar.gz

Since it's a bit of a sizeable rascal you'll probably want to ftp it
if at all possible and install the pages on your local network or box.
For those with either a fast connection or time on their hands, it is
available at all the usual sites including that at SSC:

http://www.ssc.com/lg/gazette_toc.html

Those outside the continental U.S. might want to have a look at the
mirror site page and pick a WWW or FTP site close to home:

http://www.ssc.com/lg/mirrors.html


CONTENTS:

As usual, there is a boatload of great ideas and tips and articles from
folks all over the globe (literally... :-).  These include:

    * Salutations and the MailBag
    * More 2 Cent Tips...
    * PPPD Tips -n- Tricks, by Baard Johannessen
    * Wily Editor Review, by Gary Capell
    * SNMP and Shell Scripts, by Jason Philbrook
    * Using JAVA and Netscape 2+, by Nic Tjirkalli
