		   \________//   Versatile Commodore Emulator
 		                 and Virtual Commodore Environment



A new version of VICE, the Commodore 64/128/VIC20/PET3032/4032/8032 emulator
for Unix/X, has been just released. This version provides much higher
compatibility and much better performance, particularly in the C64 section.

You can grab your copy from one of the following sites (as soon as it is moved
from the `incoming' directory):

     sunsite.unc.edu		/pub/Linux/system/Emulators
     frodo.hiof.no		/pub/emulator
     ftp.funet.fi		/pub/cbm/c64/emulation
     ftp.giga.or.at		/pub/c64/emulators/unix

     
Here are some of the new features and fixes:

  - much faster;

  - much more accurate VIC-II emulation with bad lines and correct timing;

  - completely new interrupt and CIA/VIA emulation;

  - D64 and T64 can be directly attached by the emulators (T64 in x64 and x128
    only);

  - tons of bugs fixed (keyboard and joystick included);

  - 1541 emulation improvements;

  - some new VDC features (character height, screen size, rough implementation 
    of the hires mode);

  - true shared RAM in the C128 MMU.
 

