This is a reminder that all Linux users of TeX should read Donald
Knuth's Web page <URL:http://www-cs-staff.Stanford.EDU/~knuth/cm.html>
and check their system according to the instructions given there.

Many existing Linux systems use an unauthorized version of the
Computer Modern typefaces that has been modified against the wishes of
Donald Knuth, who created these fonts originally and provided them for
free under the condition that they'll never be modified without
changing the file name, in order to ensure 100% compatibility among
all TeX installations. Many existing Linux TeX font installations
violate this requirement. This can be fixed very easily by updating
only three files. Check your system now!

Markus

