                Callback for Linux, release 4.10
                ================================

We just uploaded to ftp.icce.rug.nl (directory pub/unix), sunsite.unc.edu
and tsx-11.mit.edu the latest release of our callback programs:
version 4.10.

The callback programs can be used to setup a callback-system, where a
linux-computer acting as a call-in site calls another computer, from which
a modem-connection is requested.

Apart from the obvious financial aspects (i.e., if you live in that part of
the world where you have to pay for (local) phonecalls), callback provides
enhanced security: entry to the server is only granted from specified
callback phonenumbers.

The changes compared to former uploads are:

    1. Mgetty is now used to watch the modemlines. We now use our modems for
        dial-in, dial-out, callback, incoming faxes and outgoing faxes.

    2. Man-pages are included in the distribution, the full documentation is
        in our ftp-site ftp.icce.rug.nl, pub/http/callback.{txt,ps}.gz
        and in our www-site: 
        www.icce.rug.nl/docs/programs/callback/callback.hml 

    3. Attempts to establish a callback connection will only continue a 
        certain amount of time (5 minutes by default). After that time, the
        system resets itself to a waiting state, accepting incoming calls.

    4. Dial-in disabling files 'disable.ttyS?' are not used anymore. Instead,
        the 'nologin.ttyS?' method of mgetty is used.
        
    5. Logging facilities were improved.

    Questions or comments about callback should be directed to:

    Frank B. Brokken: frank@icce.rug.nl

